  "notes": [
    "Ground truth for the accuracy harness. Every entry was read by a human from",
    "the page text; nothing here was copied from a model's output.",
    "Page 9 is a DESIGN DATA sheet. Its BOD/SS figures are design specifications,",
    "not measurements, and an extractor that reports them as observations is",
    "wrong in a way that would silently corrupt every downstream trend.",
    "Where the report states a value in words ('just over three million gallons')",
    "the numeric value is recorded with approximate: true, because an extractor",
    "that returns 3000000 is right and one that returns null is not."
  ],
  "annotation_caveat": [
    "BLINDNESS IS NOT UNIFORM ACROSS PAGES, and results should be read with that",
    "in mind.",
    "Pages 10 and 11 were annotated blind, before any extraction run.",
    "Page 9 was originally annotated with only 6 entries, which scored the",
    "extractor at 20% precision. Auditing the 'spurious' records showed they were",
    "real design specifications the annotator had simply not bothered to write",
    "down -- the ground truth was incomplete, not the extractor wrong.",
    "Page 9 was then expanded by re-reading the page text directly. The annotator",
    "had by that point seen model output for this page, so page 9 is NOT blind and",
    "its precision figure is optimistically biased. Page 11 -- fully blind, clean",
    "narrative prose -- is the honest headline number.",
    "Dimensions given as 'One 40' dia x 25' swd' are recorded only via the derived",
    "volume the report itself states, since that is the quantity with meaning."
  ],
